# Ketos documentation

The published manual is `docs/docs`; `docs/sidebars.js` is its explicit route
inventory. Use only verified current behavior, `ketos` and `kfx` commands,
`KETOS_*` and `KFX_*` settings, `x-api-key: ${KETOS_API_KEY}` for API keys,
`Authorization: Bearer` only for JWT/OAuth tokens, and `X-KETOS-GLOBAL-VAR-*`
request variables.

Do not add upstream release history, community promotion, external OpenAPI
fetches, unverified deployment instructions, or screenshots from another
product. Retained media must be a canonical asset under `brand/assets/generated`
or a new Ketos capture with recorded OCR review.

Every page has `title` and `slug` frontmatter. Use relative links for manual
pages and fenced executable examples. Verify with:

```bash
cd docs
npm run check:links
npm run build
make api_examples_local_syntax
make api_examples_local
```

Generated OpenAPI JSON is not edited by hand. The only source generator is
`docs/openapi/generate_openapi.py`, which imports the local application.
